    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="pkg-faq">
      <details><summary>Are home removals for older people insured?</summary><p>Yes. Every Chayce removal is fully insured against loss or damage in transit, and the cover is set out in your service agreement before the move begins.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How much do removals for the elderly cost in the UK?</summary><p>Chayce packages start at &pound;995 for packing and removals and &pound;1,850 for a full-service move with a dedicated coordinator. A Discovery Consultation costs &pound;150 and gives you a personalised plan and budget first.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do you move older people long distance within the UK?</summary><p>Yes. We are based in Northampton and arrange removals across the whole UK, including long-distance moves to be closer to family.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do you only move belongings, or help with the whole move?</summary><p>Both. Bronze Essentials covers packing, removal, furniture reassembly and light cleaning, while Silver Comfort and above add declutter support, staging, deep cleaning, unpacking and a dedicated coordinator.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How far ahead should I book a removal?</summary><p>Most people begin planning three to six months ahead, but we can work to shorter timescales with a fuller-service package. Call 07708 925432 to talk through your dates.</p></details>
